      "content": "While some healthcare professionals sometimes recommend self-treatment options, such as vitamin B or steroid drops, it's important to consult a doctor before trying any treatments. High-dose vitamins and steroids can have side effects and might not be effective without professional guidance. By seeing a doctor, you can get a more accurate diagnosis and receive appropriate, safe treatment. It's always better to be cautious with these situations, even if it's just a symptom of Bell's palsy.",
      "source": "target",
